    "status": "present",
    "value": "Glasses are stacked in a triangle: row r (counting from 0) has r + 1 glasses, and each glass holds one unit. A given amount of liquid is poured into the top glass. When a glass is full, any excess splits equally into the two glasses directly below it; liquid that overflows the bottom of the tower is lost. Return how full a specified glass (row and index within the row) is, as a number between 0 and 1."
  },
